{"qid":"Q9683","names":["Tang Dynasty"],"title":"Tang Dynasty","endonym":{"native":"唐朝","lang":"zh-cn"},"capsule":"The Tang dynasty, founded in 618 when Li Yuan (Emperor Gaozu) overthrew the Sui, presided over what is often considered the apex of classical Chinese civilization, with a capital at Chang'an that was the world's largest city and a cosmopolitan entrepot for Silk Road trade. Under Emperor Taizong (r. 626–649) and Empress Wu Zetian (effective ruler 665–705, sole ruler 690–705) the empire expanded into Central Asia, Korea, and Vietnam, reaching its greatest extent under Xuanzong in the early 8th century. The An Lushan Rebellion (755–763) devastated the empire's northern heartland, killed millions, and permanently weakened central authority; the dynasty survived but never regained full control of the northwest or the military governors (jiedushi). Tang rule ended in 907 when the warlord Zhu Wen forced the last emperor to abdicate, ushering in the Five Dynasties period.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core Chinese territories are well attested by census records, administrative texts, and archaeological evidence; Central Asian tributary zones are documented by campaign records and Dunhuang manuscripts but actual governing boundaries there are conjectural; moderate confidence for the frontier zones.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Tang dynasty","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Tang-dynasty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Tang dynasty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty"}],"britannica":"topic/Tang-dynasty","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Tang dynasty","rulers":[{"qid":null,